{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"extension","externalID":"s:e:s:14GraphProtocols0A0P7CliquesE07maximalC0AD07MaximalC0VyxGyF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"roleHeading":"Extended Protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"title":"Graph","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Cliques"}],"role":"symbol"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/averageClustering()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cliqueNumber()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficient(of:)","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficients()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/coreNumbers()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/transitivity()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount(of:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols"]]},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/coreNumbers()":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"coreNumbers","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques11CoreNumbersV","text":"CoreNumbers","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"coreNumbers()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/corenumbers()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/coreNumbers()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The core decomposition of the simple graph underlying this one (self-loops ignored,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges counted once), by Batagelj–Zaversnik’s bucket algorithm. O(n + m)."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first largest clique: of all the largest cliques, the least by vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index, in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored. Of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the one holding the least vertex of their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symmetric difference. After "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cliqueNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s search, each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree. For each v, a witness clique W (any one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a candidate in W is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique among the common"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the least vertex of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the best clique so far is skipped. Up to one search per vertex and candidate, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exponential in the worst case, so it can be far slower than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":"; the search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not check for task cancellation."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstmaximumclique()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/averageClustering()":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"averageClustering"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"title":"averageClustering()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/averageclustering()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/averageClustering()","abstract":[{"text":"The mean local clustering coefficient over every vertex, zeros included, summed in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; 0 when empty.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between them.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"symbol","title":"Graph","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/triangleCount()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of triangles in the simple graph. O(m^(3\/2))."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/trianglecount()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount()","title":"triangleCount()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"triangleCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/clusteringCoefficient(of:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficient(of:)","abstract":[{"text":"The local clustering coefficient of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex"},{"text":", from its neighborhood alone: 2T \/ (d(d − 1)),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 when it has fewer than two distinct neighbors.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clusteringCoefficient","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"clusteringCoefficient(of:)","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/clusteringcoefficient(of:)"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/transitivity()":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/transitivity()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/transitivity()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Three times the triangles over the connected triples; 0 when there are no triangles."}],"title":"transitivity()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transitivity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; see ","type":"text"},{"code":"MaximalCliques","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one.","type":"text"}],"title":"maximalCliques()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalCliques","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumClique()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A largest clique of the simple graph, in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Deterministic, but which largest clique it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"depends on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It is the clique "},{"code":"cliqueNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s search finds, so it costs the same: exponential in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"worst case, memory O(n + m + degeneracy²). The search does not check for task cancellation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumclique()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()","title":"maximumClique()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumClique","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/triangleCount(of:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount(of:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The number of triangles through ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", from its neighborhood alone.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"triangleCount"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"title":"triangleCount(of:)","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/trianglecount(of:)"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/cliqueNumber()":{"abstract":[{"text":"The size of a largest clique of the simple graph, ω: 0 for the empty graph, 1 for an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edgeless one, at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracy + 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Branch and bound in degeneracy order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each vertex’s later neighbors (at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"degeneracy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those with a high enough core number)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the candidates, one search per vertex that raises the best size as it goes, stopping at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the degeneracy bound. Each search is San Segundo et al.’s BBMC on bitsets, candidates in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"descending degree, branching from the highest greedy colour down. Exponential in the worst","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"case; memory O(n + m + degeneracy²).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/cliquenumber()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cliqueNumber()","kind":"symbol","title":"cliqueNumber()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cliqueNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/clusteringCoefficients()":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficients()","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Triangles and clustering for every vertex of the simple graph (self-loops ignored,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges counted once), in one compact-forward pass. O(m^(3\/2))."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clusteringCoefficients"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques22ClusteringCoefficientsV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ClusteringCoefficients"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"clusteringCoefficients()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/clusteringcoefficients()"}}}